<p>SCP-5545-3 is a phenomenon resulting in SCP-5545-2's interactions with SCP-5545-1. During this process, SCP-5545-1's area of effect will exponentially increase with time, resulting in the manifestation of SCP-5545-1 occurring globally within a period of 4–6 hours. This will continue so as long as SCP-5545-2 is present within SCP-5545-1; subversively, SCP-5545-1 will logarithmically decrease in its area of effect while SCP-5545-2 is not present within it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, but if it can only be entered via Site-344-1, why does this matter? How do they know it extends globally if there's only one entrance and exit?<br />
(also I think you meant &quot;resulting from&quot;)<br />
The use of &quot;arctic&quot; was odd, given that it's in Antarctica. Also, the references to &quot;night&quot; and &quot;day&quot; by Monroe (in November there it's light for 24 hours a day), though that could be explained by an artificial day-night lighting cycle within the site.</p>
<p>Regarding the reincarnation: does Monroe reincarnate as an adult of the same age every time? Speaking the same language? Does he have a memetic effect that everyone (including himself) has memories of his life up to the moment he &quot;appeared&quot;? Or he retroactively always existed? Does that mean the murder he committed happens again and again? Does he just appear out of whole cloth, or does the body he inhabits exist as someone else until it's time, morphing physically and mentally to become Jason Monroe?</p>
<p>One more typo:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>made me realize was I was standing in front of</p>
</blockquote>

